From 47cb6d2f7e71012eefac228434900e069a34655e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:26:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] WebCore: its Ruby generators as Python, so the browser builds
 without Ruby

generate-abstract-heap.rb, GenerateSettings.rb (five templates) and
GenerateQuirkBehaviors.rb (four templates) have Python 3 ports beside them,
standard library only. The templates have Python forms (.pyerb), rendered by
GeneratePreferences.py's ERB-subset renderer; its YAML reader now also reads
block scalars (| and >) and block sequences of scalars, which Settings.yaml
and DOMJITAbstractHeapRepository.yaml use. On AmigaOS, WebCore's CMake runs
the Python scripts; with this, no build step of the Amiga port runs Ruby.

The ten outputs (DOMJITAbstractHeapRepository.h, Settings.h, Settings.cpp,
InternalSettingsGenerated.h/.cpp/.idl, QuirkBehaviorDefinitions.h,
QuirkBehaviorID.h, QuirksAccessors.h/.cpp) match the Ruby scripts' byte for
byte on the 5 October build's inputs.
